==============================================================================
LineageOS 20.0 / Android system and vendor images for the Waydroid
container
  system.img
  vendor.img
==============================================================================

These two images are prebuilt binaries fetched from the Waydroid OTA
channel on SourceForge:

  system.img   lineage-20.0-20260403-VANILLA-waydroid_x86_64-system.zip
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/waydroid/files/images/system/lineage/
        waydroid_x86_64/
  vendor.img   lineage-20.0-20260428-MAINLINE-waydroid_x86_64-vendor.zip
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/waydroid/files/images/vendor/
        waydroid_x86_64/

Everything below is reproduced from the notices that ship inside those
images.  Attribution for the Waydroid project itself (the container
tooling) is separate and does not cover the image contents, which are
AOSP and LineageOS builds with a large amount of third-party material -
MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, GPL-2, MPL and zlib among others.

   =========================================================================
   ==  Notice of modification, per section 4 b of                         ==
   ==  the Apache License, Version 2.0.                                   ==
   =========================================================================

vendor.img is shipped unmodified.

system.img is shipped with one modification, made by NAVER Corporation:

    /system/framework/org.lineageos.platform.jar
        two bytes inside classes.dex
    /system/framework/oat/x86_64/org.lineageos.platform.odex   removed
    /system/framework/oat/x86_64/org.lineageos.platform.vdex   removed

IPlatform.removeApp() built a PendingIntent with FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT but
with neither FLAG_IMMUTABLE nor FLAG_MUTABLE.  Android 12 and later
reject that combination, so every app uninstall threw
IllegalArgumentException.  installApp() in the same class already sets
FLAG_IMMUTABLE; the edit makes removeApp() match it.  The two AOT
sidecars are dropped because they embed a hash of the pre-edit
classes.dex and would otherwise keep being used.

org.lineageos.platform.jar is part of the LineageOS SDK and is licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0, which permits modification and
asks only that the change be stated - this notice.  No GPL- or
LGPL-covered component of either image is modified; the GPL-2 material
in system.img (OpenJDK under com.android.art, the f2fs-tools binaries
and the hyphenation data) is byte-identical to upstream.

   =========================================================================
   ==  Source of this text                                                ==
   =========================================================================

Extracted from the images themselves:

    system.img : /system/etc/NOTICE.xml.gz
                 md5 b21236ec86c4188856bd7d0b5c8244d0
                 378 license blocks covering 5091 files
    vendor.img : /etc/NOTICE.xml.gz
                 md5 a608a44ab5ee64e2fb5b0ca54e9eb699
                 93 license blocks covering 2259 files

Identical license texts share one Android contentId, so the 471 blocks
of the two files reduce to the 418 unique blocks reproduced below; each
is tagged with the image or images it applies to.  The per-file index
that maps each of the 7350 paths to its contentId is not reproduced
here - the unmodified NOTICE.xml.gz files are installed on the device at

    /usr/share/waydroid-extra/NOTICE/

so the mapping can be recovered and this text can be checked against the
original.

